course: dictionary
lesson: 8606
title: Scrabble: clawing, struggling, and a game
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Scrabble is a verb and a noun. As a verb, to scrabble means to scratch or grope about quickly with your hands or claws, looking for something or trying to hold on. In «he scraped and scratched and scrabbled and scrooged», the words around scrabble are all digging words, so it must be a kind of quick, busy digging.
explain: Use the clues. Mole is digging his tunnel, and he mutters «Up we go!», so he is pushing upwards through the earth. Scrabble must mean clawing or scratching at the ground. Check it by swapping in your meaning: «he scraped and scratched and scratched and scrooged» still makes sense.
explain: Scrabble can also mean to struggle or hurry to get something. Alice scrabbles to keep hold: she is not calmly holding on, she is fighting to stay where she is. The second meaning keeps the same feeling of quick, frantic movement.
explain: A capital S changes the word. Scrabble, with a capital letter, is a board game. Players make words with letter tiles and score points. When a word starts with a capital letter, check whether it is a name before you guess its meaning.
fact: Scrabble is a verb: scrabble, scrabbles, scrabbled, scrabbling.
fact: «Scrabble» means to scratch or grope about quickly with your hands or claws.
fact: «Scrabble» can also mean to struggle or hurry to get something.
fact: Scrabble with a capital S is a board game where players make words with letter tiles and score points.
fact: Context clue: a capital letter at the start of a word often shows a name, such as the game Scrabble.
exercise: «He scraped and scratched and scrabbled and scrooged.» What does scrabbled mean here? | Sang a loud song | Sat down and rested | Painted a picture | *Scratched or grabbed quickly with hands or claws
exercise: «Alice scrabbles to keep hold.» What is Alice doing? | Calmly sitting and reading | Lets go and falls asleep | Drawing a picture of the sky | *Struggling quickly to hang on
exercise: Scrabble, with a capital S, is what kind of thing? | A tall tower | A dance | *A board game with letter tiles | A kind of fruit
test: Mole «scrabbles» up from his home. What is he doing? | Dancing in a circle | *Digging and clawing his way upwards | Flying in the sky | Lazily sleeping in bed
test: Which sentence uses Scrabble as a board game? | *We played Scrabble at home and I scored forty points. | He scrabbled in his pocket for a coin. | Alice scrabbled to keep hold. | Animals scrabble at the earth.
exam: Why does the capital S in Scrabble matter? | It tells you to shout the word | *It shows a name, the board game, not the action of scrabbling | It shows the word is a question | It means the word is very old
